    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d31">

                <pb facs="0094" n="22" xml:id="pg22"/>

                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Marquis d’Abrantes
                        to General Webb</hi>.</head>
                <note rend="inline" rendition="#center" type="source">[Translation.]</note>
                <dateline>
                    <placeName>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Botafoga</hi></placeName>, <date
                        calendar="gregorian" when="1865-05-21">
                        <hi rendition="#italic">May</hi> 21, 1865</date>.</dateline>
                <p>
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">My Dear General</hi>: Allow me to fulfil the painful
                    duty to manifest to you my deep personal sorrow on the deplorable event which
                    has deprived your country of her so highly distinguished President, Mr.
                    Lincoln.</p>
                <p>But it may be said that the horrible act which has brought to a close his
                    existence has heightened him still more in the thankful citizens of the United
                    States, and insures him a still more renowned name in history.</p>
                <p>In wishing to your great and fair country every prosperity, I remain, with the
                    most perfect esteem and consideration, my dear general, your friend,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>ABRANTES.</signed>
                </closer>
                <postscript>
                    <p>J. <hi rendition="#small-caps">Watson Webb</hi>, Esq., <hi
                            rendition="#italic">Minister of the United States</hi>.</p>
                </postscript>
            </div>
        </body>
